WS2 Milestone B: python-driven irq stimulus through the UVM irq agent
=======================================================================

Command (Task 7 brief's Step 3, run as committed):

  ( cd dv/uvm/core_ibex && make SIMULATOR=vcs IBEX_CONFIG=opentitan ISS=spike \
    TEST=cocotb_irq_python_test ITERATIONS=1 SEED=1 COCOTB=1 \
    COCOTB_MODULE=dv.cocotb.tests.test_irq_from_python OUT=out_mb )

Design summary
--------------
- rtl_test stays core_ibex_base_test; no +enable_irq_*_seq sim_opts are set, so the stock SV irq
  sequences never start. All irq timing comes from cocotb's uvm_bridge.trigger("cocotb_irq_raise")
  DPI calls, turned into a raise-then-drop pulse by an armed uvm_event listener
  (core_ibex_base_test.sv's cocotb_irq_listener, forked first in run_phase so it arms before
  send_stimulus() starts) driving fresh cocotb_irq_raise_seq/irq_drop_seq objects through the real
  irq_agent sequencer (core_ibex_vseq.sv).
- Handler-entry counter (cocotb_if.handler_entry_count, core_ibex_tb_top.sv) increments on cycles
  where controller_state == ibex_pkg::IRQ_TAKEN -- the controller's single-cycle-per-entry state
  for taking an interrupt (already used by a pre-existing WARNING check in the same file), not raw
  irq_vif line toggles, so it counts actual trap entries, not stimulus edges that may never be
  serviced (e.g. while globally masked).
- Checked BEFORE finish(), not after: the flow's log scanner
  (ibex_log_to_trace_csv.check_ibex_uvm_log) stops treating "Error" lines as failures once it has
  seen "RISC-V UVM TEST PASSED" in the log. That banner only appears once the whole generated
  program (+instr_cnt=10000) reaches its own riscv-dv signature handshake at natural completion,
  well after our own irq activity finishes -- asserting after finish() would silently land past
  that point and never be able to fail the flow. Checked right after the trigger loop (plus a
  short settle wait) instead, the check always lands before that banner.

