Negative control (Step 4, mutation-style named-checker ablation)
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Same command, fresh OUT, with the ONE line
`dv/uvm/core_ibex/riscv_dv_extension/testlist.yaml`'s cocotb_irq_python_test sim_opts temporarily
edited from `+cocotb_irq_count=3` to `+cocotb_irq_count=0` (reverted after capture; never
committed in that state) -- i.e. cocotb sends zero irq triggers while
_MIN_EXPECTED_HANDLER_ENTRIES stays fixed at 3 in test_irq_from_python.py (deliberately NOT tied
to the plusarg, so this ablation actually exercises the checker instead of trivially passing
`0 >= 0`). Result: `handler_entry_count=0`, the assertion fires, and -- because it fires before
finish() -- cocotb's own uncaught-exception handling $finishes immediately, so
"RISC-V UVM TEST PASSED" never has a chance to print at all this run:

  2.00ns INFO     cocotb    COCOTB-IRQ: cocotb_irq_count=0 (seed=1)
  2044.35ns INFO  cocotb    COCOTB-IRQ: uvm_ready observed
  12044.36ns INFO cocotb    COCOTB-IRQ: handler_entry_count=0 (triggered=0, required>=3)
  12044.36ns INFO cocotb.regression   test_irq_from_python failed
  Traceback (most recent call last):
    File ".../dv/cocotb/tests/test_irq_from_python.py", line 77, in test_irq_from_python
      assert count >= _MIN_EXPECTED_HANDLER_ENTRIES, (
  AssertionError: COCOTB-IRQ-CHECK: handler_entry_count=0 is below the required 3
  (triggered 0 times); irq stimulus was not serviced
  ** dv.cocotb.tests.test_irq_from_python.test_irq_from_python   FAIL   12044.36 ...
  $finish at simulation time              1204436

Flow-level verdict (regr.log / trr.yaml), proving this is a real flow FAIL, not just a cocotb-side
one:

  0.00% PASS 0 PASSED, 1 FAILED
  cocotb_irq_python_test.1: FAILED
  [FAILED]: error seen in 'rtl_sim_stdstreams.log'
  ---------------*LOG-EXTRACT*----------------
  [E] 54: AssertionError: COCOTB-IRQ-CHECK: handler_entry_count=0 is below the required 3
      (triggered 0 times); irq stimulus was not serviced
  --------------------------------------------
  trr.yaml: failure_mode: LOG_ERROR(3)
  make exit code: 2

This proves THIS check (not cosim, not a generic UVM_ERROR) fires and fails the test when the irq
stimulus it is supposed to attribute handler entries to never happens. Broken run's artifacts
(fresh OUT, not committed) removed after capture.

Bug found and fixed along the way (documented in Task 7 report,
docs/dv/process-logs/ws2/task-7-report.md): the assertion message originally
contained an em-dash (U+2014). cocotb's own failure-logging path uses an ASCII-only stream
encoder; that character crashed the log call with UnicodeEncodeError, which silently swallowed the
AssertionError text and caused this exact negative control to show a false flow-level PASS on the
first attempt, despite cocotb itself correctly scoring the test FAIL. Fixed by keeping all
runtime-logged/raised strings in dv/cocotb/ plain ASCII; re-ran and confirmed the FAIL above.

