Fix round 1 (review response) -- re-verification
=================================================
Review found 3 Important findings: a vacuous-pass hazard when COCOTB=0, an overstated
"no lost triggers" claim (uvm_event.trigger() is not queued -- a trigger arriving while the
listener is still mid-pulse is dropped), and an unenforced 1:1 correspondence between triggers
and handler entries. Fixes: a build_phase uvm_fatal when +cocotb_irq_count is seen without
COCOTB_SIM compiled in; a trigger_received_count counter (core_ibex_cocotb_if.sv/
core_ibex_base_test.sv) that Python compares against its own triggers-sent count before finish();
the handler-entry assertion now requires max(n, 3) (still failing the ablation at n=0) and logs a
loud WARNING if handler_entry_count exceeds triggers_sent (over-count attribution, non-fatal).
testlist iterations pinned to 1 (single-seed-tuned timing). Full detail:
docs/dv/process-logs/ws2/task-7-report.md.

